      gas absorbs red light, giving Uranus its pale cyan, tranquil hue.
    diameter: 50,724 km
    distanceFromSun: 2.87 Billion km (19.2 AU)
    orbitalPeriod: 84 Earth Years
    surfaceTemperature: "-224\xB0C (Coldest atmosphere)"
    interestingFact: Uranus rolls on its side with an axial tilt of nearly 98 degrees,
      likely caused by an ancient cataclysmic collision with an Earth-sized protoplanet!
